ction over 2–3 min (to terminate PSVT), 60–120 mg TDS orally for maintenance and to control ventricular rate in atrial fibrillation or flutter","b":"Calaptin"},{"n":"Diltiazem","d":"25 mg by slow i.v. inj (to terminate PSVT and to rapidly control ventricular rate in atrial fibrillation or flutter), 30–60 mg TDS orally for maintenance","b":"Dilzem"}]},{"name":"Drugs for PSVT","drugs":[{"n":"Adenosine","d":"6–12 mg (free base) by rapid i.v. injection in a central vein","b":"Adenoject, Adenocor"},{"n":"Digoxin","d":"0.25–0.5 mg/day (elderly 0.125–0.25 mg/day) oral adjusted according to response, 0.25 mg slow i.v. injection followed by 0.1 mg 1–2 hourly as needed","b":"Lanoxin, Cardioxin, Dixin"}]}]},"footnote":"PSVT: Paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia."}]}